# Supabase (hosted project, not self-run - there is no local Supabase
# container in this repo's Docker setup).
#
# NOT YET WIRED IN: src/integrations/supabase/client.ts still hardcodes the
# project URL and anon/publishable key directly (see docs/TECHNICAL_DEBT.md
# item 5 and docs/IMPROVEMENT_ROADMAP.md's Phase 5/Phase 9 entries). That
# migration ("read from import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL /
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY instead of the literals") is explicitly Phase 9's
# job, not this phase's - this file only reserves the variable names/shape
# Phase 9 will wire client.ts to read from, per the already-approved Phase 3
# plan. Setting these now has no effect on the current build.
#
# The current hardcoded value is Supabase's anon/publishable key (JWT
# "role":"anon"), not a service-role key - by Supabase's own design this
# key is meant to be client-exposed and is not a secret to rotate (RLS
# policies are the real access boundary). See docs/REPOSITORY_AUDIT.md's
# secret-scan section for the full classification and its one open caveat
# (RLS coverage is only confirmed for the 2 version-controlled tables;
# P0 #3 in docs/TECHNICAL_DEBT.md tracks the rest, owned by Phase 9).
# Placeholders only (CLAUDE.md: ".env.example" carries placeholders, never
# real values, even for a client-safe anon key) - see src/integrations/
# supabase/client.ts for the value actually in effect today.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=<https-your-project-ref.supabase.co>
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<supabase-anon-public-key>

# Docker-only, non-secret: host port docker-compose publishes the app on.
# Defaults to 20070 (this repo's reserved block is 20070-20079). Not read
# by the app itself - compose/Makefile only.
HOST_PORT=20070
